        <groundspeak:log id="654347850">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-12-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="4650656">Safari Cachers</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP536 - SAW2 Police Point&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What an action packed 2 days!   We left Calgary at 6:30AM on Friday morning and I got home at 9PM Saturday night.  All told, we put on 1400 kms and found over 200 caches.  My co-pilot and navigator were pickledherrings (The Sister) and UBOFF.  We found oldies, we found newies, we found everything in between.  The goal was a couple of power trails near Speedy Creek.  We finished one and put a huge dent in the other. (Call it a pre-cursor to the Mega event next summer).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks to all the C.O's for the great caches that we encountered, and thanks to pickledherrings and UBOFF for the awesome time.  My belly still hurts from all the laughs and jabs...and I still can't hear out of one ear (too many horn blasts)....&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TFTC!!!!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
